  "notes": [
    "Wowhead Classic spell pages (classic/spell=<id>) have NO 'Taught by NPC' / 'Learned from' listview for these pet abilities; only 'Used by Pet' (families) and 'See also' (other ranks). Rank spell IDs and 'Requires level N' (recorded as petLevel) come from those pages. Wowhead shows no TP cost.",
    "Wowhead Classic NPC pages: the one page fetched (npc=3121 Durotar Tiger: 'Level: 7 - 8', Durotar, 'Tameable (Cat)') does not list the abilities the beast teaches; further NPC page fetches were then blocked by Wowhead (HTTP 403 'Request blocked'), so no Wowhead beast observations were recorded and elite/rare flags could not be taken from Wowhead.",
    "Wowhead has a Forever section (search results show wowhead.com/forever/... NPC URLs) but every /forever/ page returned HTTP 403 to both curl and WebFetch; no wowhead-forever data recorded.",
    "warcraft.wiki.gg ability pages give only general data (rank count, base level, some spell IDs in external-link headers, icon); no per-rank TP costs and no beast lists. The wiki's Beast Training page states Cower, Dash and Prowl are learned from tamed beasts (not pet trainers), hence trainerOnly=false.",
    "petopia-classic = https://www.wow-petopia.com/classic/abilities.php (one page, anchors per rank). Gives pet level + TP per rank and beasts with (classic.wowhead.com) NPC IDs, family, level range, zone. No elite/rare flags. No spell IDs (null).",
    "warcrafttavern = warcrafttavern.com WoW Classic hunter-pet model pages (per beast: Pet Level, 'Skills When Tamed', Zone). No NPC IDs; matched to Petopia's IDs by exact name. Probably compiled from the same community data as Petopia, but it differs in places (see notes below), so it is recorded as a separate source; the generator may want to weight it as partially dependent on Petopia. Zone strings are recorded as shown, including site typos (e.g. 'Eastern Plagulands', 'Ferelas'). Its hunter-pet-abilities guide links one spell ID per ability for the max rank (16698 Cower, 23112 Dash, 24455 Prowl); these differ from the Wowhead pet-spell IDs and look like the Beast Training 'teach' spell variants. Recorded as-is in the warcrafttavern rank observation, unverified.",
    "No source that loaded showed elite/rare flags, so elite/rare are omitted. Nothing Forever-specific was found; all data is the Classic Era baseline. (The wiki's Cower page says the ability 'remains in Classic and Forever'.)",
    "Petopia rank data: pet levels 5/15/25/35/45/55, TP 8/10/12/14/16/18. Wowhead 'Requires level' matches the levels.",
    "Kraul Bat, Greater Kraul Bat (Razorfen Kraul) and Shrike Bat (Uldaman) are dungeon beasts per both sources.",
    "warcraft.wiki.gg Beast Training page says a tamed Durotar Tiger knows Cower (Rank 1) when tamed; recorded as a wiki observation for npc 3121 (no level/zone given there)."
